# The Sanity Studio is a separate, standalone app (its own package.json/
# node_modules, deployed independently via `sanity deploy` if at all) — it
# has nothing to do with this Next.js app's runtime. Vercel's zero-config
# build otherwise notices its package.json and tries to resolve its
# dependency tree too, which fails on an unrelated peer-dependency conflict
# in the Studio's own toolchain.
studio

# Real config lives in Vercel's own env var UI/CLI (see .env.example for the
# full list) — these local files should never ride along in an uploaded
# deployment even though .gitignore already keeps them out of git itself.
.env
.env.local
